A_652 - Chickens are also considered pets, and chicken coops aren't cruel if they're spacious enough and well-maintained. It might seem so, but the truth is that chickens, even when released from the coop, return to sleep there in the evening. If freedom were more precious to them, they would escape into the countryside, taking advantage of their freedom, never to return. However, it's true that chickens often have their wings clipped, so to resolve this issue, they shouldn't be mutilated in the first place ...